Session 5 – Naive Pattern Matching
Task 9: String Matching in an Array – LeetCode
Approach
Check whether each word is a substring of another word.
import java.util.*;

class Solution {

    public List<String> stringMatching(String[] words) {

        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>();

        for (int i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {

            for (int j = 0; j < words.length; j++) {

                if (i != j &&
                    words[j].contains(words[i])) {

                    result.add(words[i]);
                    break;
                }
            }
        }

        return result;
    }
}
Example
Input:
["mass","as","hero","superhero"]

Output:
["as","hero"]
Because:
"as" is inside "mass"
"hero" is inside "superhero"
